{"chunk_id": "02348d43ac0f", "text": "Markandeya describes the catastrophic end of the current Yuga, when moral order collapses and cosmic disturbances signal the breakdown of the world. Social bonds decay: disciples defy teachers, families turn violent, charity disappears, and people wander in desperation amid famine, fires, eclipses, and ominous celestial signs. Nature itself reflects disorder with unseasonal rains, dim stars, and blazing horizons. Yet the destruction is not final. After this chaos, creation renews and the Krita (Satya) age begins. A Brahmana named Kalki is born in Sambhala, empowered with divine weapons and devoted to Vishnu. He destroys thieves, robbers, and impious peoples, restores righteousness, performs a great horse sacrifice, and reestablishes sacred social order. With virtue revived, agriculture prospers, rituals return, and society realigns with dharma, marking the cyclical rebirth of a just world.\nMarkandeya describes Kalki restoring order after Kali Yuga, inaugurating a renewed Krita age of virtue, prosperity, and restored social-religious order.\nThemes: Kalki avatar, end of Kali Yuga, cosmic renewal, restoration of dharma, cyclical time", "vector": [0.005841451231390238, -0.02112562023103237, 0.002542270114645362, 0.00037697047810070217, -0.015572678297758102, 9.408351616002619e-05, -0.0237323809415102, -0.015436909161508083, -0.008974315598607063, -0.013033801689743996, 0.021288543939590454, 0.026692140847444534, -0.0004866461968049407, 0.0237323809415102, -0.00936125684529543, -0.006645881105214357, 0.04116509109735489, -0.004782455042004585, 0.012640072964131832, -0.007236475590616465, -0.00836335588246584, 0.027004407718777657, 0.0053221359848976135, -0.014486528001725674, -0.011526769027113914, 0.024302609264850616, 0.013067743740975857, -0.02456057071685791, 0.020582545548677444, 0.0051592132076621056, -0.007087129633873701, -0.017296941950917244, -0.007270417641848326, 0.010196235030889511, -0.030140666291117668, -0.010359156